Makitra(*) is a simple, intuitive electronic recipe book. This is a substitute for the paper notebook with recipes that many housewives and home cooks have or had.

The application allows you to write down recipes, make notes on them, edit them based on your taste preferences or the characteristics of the products of the region, and share recipes with friends or relatives.
The main task of the application is to be simple, convenient and not overloaded with unnecessary functions.

Features:
- adding your photo to the description of the recipe;
- automatic calculation of ingredients amount, if you need to cook more / less than 1 serving;
- adding any number of recipes;
- grouping recipes into different categories;
- support of the cooking process:
    - you can mark the stages that have already been completed;
    - set a timer directly in the application and receive a notification when the time is up;
- simultaneous preparation of several dishes, with control over what has already been done in which recipe and what has not.
- sharing recipes via AirDrop or email;

Use it on iPhone or iPad (recipe list is synchronized via iCloud).

* Makіtra is a national Ukrainian cone-shaped bowl made of clay, in which poppy seeds were ground, dough came up or various products were crushed.

